in @prism
in @meta
in @io
in @option
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/property
in @epistemologic/property/content_addressed

# @epistemologic/silicon/compute_bound
#
# A compute budget representation. Names the upper limits a peer is
# allowed to consume when it runs inside a shard: CPU cores, host
# memory, GPU memory, wall-clock time, spectral reductions.
#
# Per docs/specs/shard-design.md §6: the carrier the shard's
# `compute` field holds. Per the same §6: bounds are enforced at the
# `spawn` boundary via `@mirror/shard.admits(host, child)`; a peer
# requesting more than the host shard's compute_bound allows fails
# the type check BEFORE the gen_prism ticks. Per-agent sandboxing
# without runtime trapping.
#
# Every field is option(T) for two reasons. First, the system's
# hard maxima (returned by detect_max) populate every field, but a
# user-declared budget in a shard manifest typically constrains
# only a subset — leaving the rest at the parent shard's value via
# intersection. Second, the GPU field is genuinely absent on
# silicon without a GPU; option encodes that honestly.
#
# Per Task #74: max_reductions is the budget the spectral-reductions
# halting mechanism reads. A bounded reductions field gives the
# substrate a structural halting argument; unbounded (none) gives
# the conventional Turing-complete posture.

grammar @epistemologic/silicon/compute_bound {

  # Wall-clock time as milliseconds. Declared locally rather than
  # imported from @beam.duration to keep the silicon carriers from
  # pulling the full BEAM runtime grammar; compute_bound is a
  # silicon-level concern, not a BEAM concern. Design call parked:
  # promote to a shared @time.duration if a second silicon carrier
  # needs the same representation.
  type wall_time = u64

  # The compute_bound carrier. Five fields, all option-typed:
  #
  #   max_cpu_cores       upper bound on CPU parallelism.
  #   max_memory_bytes    upper bound on host RAM allocation.
  #   max_gpu_memory_bytes upper bound on GPU/accelerator VRAM.
  #                       none on silicon without a GPU.
  #   max_wall_time       upper bound on wall-clock execution
  #                       (in milliseconds). none = unbounded.
  #   max_reductions      upper bound on spectral-reductions before
  #                       the substrate forces a halt (per Task #74).
  #                       none = unbounded.
  #
  # Five fields matches the Prism algebra's cardinality — each
  # bound corresponds to one axis of resource extraction the shard
  # rations: parallelism (split), memory (project), accelerator
  # (zoom), time (focus), settlement (refract).
  type compute_bound = {
    max_cpu_cores:        option(u32),
    max_memory_bytes:     option(u64),
    max_gpu_memory_bytes: option(u64),
    max_wall_time:        option(wall_time),
    max_reductions:       option(u64),
  }

  requires content_addressed(compute_bound)

  # Detection primitive. Returns the system's HARD MAXIMA — not a
  # budget. A budget is allocated by the shard's `admits` action
  # (shard-design §6); detect_max names the ceiling the budget
  # cannot exceed.
  #
  # max_cpu_cores from hw.ncpu (Darwin) / nproc (Linux).
  # max_memory_bytes from hw.memsize / /proc/meminfo.
  # max_gpu_memory_bytes from system_profiler SPDisplaysDataType
  # (Darwin) / nvidia-smi --query-gpu=memory.total (Linux); some
  # for the vendor SDK that responds, none otherwise.
  # max_wall_time is none from the hardware (the user controls it).
  # max_reductions is none from the hardware (the substrate sets it).
  #
  # Body is a Fate-resolved hole; the tournament picks the right
  # detection chain for the running OS + GPU vendor at boot.
  detect_max() -> compute_bound { \ }

  # Literal property. Same discipline as the other silicon carriers:
  # re-detect, content-address, compare. The max values are stable
  # across a kernel session (hotplug aside) so the OID equality holds.
  property literal(b: compute_bound) -> verdict { \ }
}

out compute_bound
out wall_time
out detect_max
out literal
out @epistemologic/silicon/compute_bound
